        "Name": "Bubble Point",
        "ID": "BubblePoint",
        "Description": "The Bubble Point is the temperature and pressure at which a hydrocarbon liquid mixture, when heated or depressurized, begins to produce bubbles of gas. It represents the onset of gas formation in a liquid-dominated system under equilibrium conditions.",
